Hold frames at startup while a monitor keeps the picture from before us

When something else had the screen before Hyprland, e.g. a boot splash
whose last frame the backend kept (aquamarine's AQ_SPLASH_ADOPT), the first
frames Hyprland presents show its own startup state, such as an empty
workspace or a half-faded layer, before the session's cover appears.

misc:startup_hold_layer (level:namespace, empty by default) names a layer
surface. From the first frame until one with that namespace is mapped on
that layer level of the monitor and opaque, a monitor whose output still
shows the picture from before us presents nothing, so the picture stays.
Each monitor is released on its own. misc:startup_hold_timeout (ms, 5000)
releases every monitor still held, for a layer that never comes. A
released monitor never holds again. A monitor the backend kept no picture
on (no adoption, another mode, a later disable or mode change) renders as
before, so the hold never keeps an unrendered frame of ours on screen.

Needs IOutput::showsAdoptedPicture() from aquamarine's AQ_SPLASH_ADOPT
patch.

Not yet upstream.

